<div class="book-title">Likutay Halachos — Orach Chaim</div>
<div class="halacha-title">Hilchos Netilas Yadayim L'Seudah U'Betzi'as HaPas 4</div>
<div class="part-label">Part 2 — Sections 4–10, including Betzi'as HaPas</div>

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<!-- Section 4 (source: אות ד) — Water Purifies     -->
<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<div class="section-number">§ 4 — Why Water Purifies from All Impurities</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  And for this reason, <span class="key-concept">water purifies from all impurities</span>. And it is impossible to enter into any holiness without water — such as the <span class="heb-term">Kohanim</span> in their [Temple] service. And similarly, in the morning upon rising. And similarly, before prayer and Torah study, one needs to immerse or wash one's hands with water. And similarly, all the ritually impure do not ascend from their impurity except through water.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  For water symbolizes the <span class="heb-term">da'as</span> of the renewal of the world. For water preceded all of creation — for the beginning of creation was water, as our Sages, of blessed memory, said. It emerges that the primary renewal of the world began from water. And therefore, there is the primary root of the <span class="heb-term">da'as</span> of the renewal of the world — through which the primary purification [is accomplished]. And only through this does one enter the service of Hashem. For this is the primary foundation of the holy <span class="heb-term">emunah</span> — to believe in the renewal of the world, in the aspect of: <span class="verse">"In the beginning, G-d created the heavens"</span> etc. — which is the beginning of the Torah.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  And this is the primary holiness and purity. For conversely, all the impurities are drawn from the <span class="heb-term">zuhamas hanachash</span> [contamination of the serpent], which brought death — from which the primary impurity [comes]. And the primary [aspect] of the contamination of the serpent is the heresy of those who deny the renewal of the world, G-d forbid. And therefore, water — which is the aspect of the waters of <span class="heb-term">da'as</span> mentioned above, through which the <span class="heb-term">emunah</span> of the renewal of the world is drawn — through this, [one achieves] all the purifications in the world. And it is impossible to enter any holiness or service except through water. For all holiness and all service of Hashem depend on this <span class="heb-term">emunah</span> of the renewal of the world — which one merits to draw upon oneself through purification in water, through immersion or washing, according to the law. For through purification in water, one draws upon oneself the aspect of the illumination of the waters of <span class="heb-term">da'as</span> that will be revealed in the future — through which one merits the <span class="heb-term">emunah</span> of the renewal of the world, which is the foundation of the Torah and of service, as mentioned above.
</div>

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<!-- Section 5 (source: אות ה) — Tisha B'Av         -->
<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<div class="section-number">§ 5 — The Four Fasts, Tisha B'Av, and <i>Shabbos Chazon</i></div>

<div class="paragraph">
  And this is the aspect of the <span class="key-concept">four fasts</span> over the destruction of the <span class="heb-term">Bais HaMikdash</span> — which was caused by the sin of the spies, who wept on the night of <span class="heb-term">Tisha B'Av</span>, who blemished <span class="heb-term">Eretz Yisrael</span> — where the <span class="heb-term">emunah</span> of the renewal of the world is revealed. And they blemished this. Through this, the <span class="heb-term">zuhamas hanachash</span> — <span class="heb-term">mezona d'gufa</span> — intensified, G-d forbid, as mentioned above. Therefore one needs to fast, in order to subdue the <span class="heb-term">mezona d'gufa</span>.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  For when one merits complete <span class="heb-term">emunah</span>, one does not need to fast. For through <span class="heb-term">emunah</span>, the eating is in the aspect of <span class="heb-term">mezona d'nishmesa</span> — which is the aspect of the eating of upright Jews, the aspect of eating on Shabbos. For through <span class="heb-term">emunah</span>, the primary refinement of eating [is accomplished], as is explained elsewhere, in the aspect of: <span class="verse">"and graze on <span class="heb-term">emunah</span>"</span> <span class="source-ref">(Psalms 37:3)</span>. But because they blemished <span class="heb-term">Eretz Yisrael</span> and blemished the <span class="heb-term">emunah</span>, as mentioned above — therefore one needs to fast, to subdue the <span class="heb-term">mezona d'gufa</span> through the fast.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  And this is the aspect of <span class="heb-term">Eichah</span> [Lamentations] that we recite on <span class="heb-term">Tisha B'Av</span>. And this is the aspect of: <span class="verse">"<span class="heb-term">Eichah</span> — how the gold has become dim"</span> <span class="source-ref">(Lamentations 4:1)</span>. For the primary [subject of] the lamentations is over the <span class="key-concept">passing of the true <span class="heb-term">tzadikim</span></span> — which is twice as [devastating as] the destruction of the <span class="heb-term">Bais HaMikdash</span>. And through this, we are now like <span class="verse">"sheep that have no shepherd."</span> For we do not know who the true <span class="heb-term">tzadik</span> is. And we need to cry out and search and seek: "<span class="heb-term">Eichah</span>! <span class="heb-term">Eichah</span>! [Where?! Where?!]" — [seeking] the true <span class="heb-term">tzadik</span> whose light has been darkened for us, for we do not merit to know of him. And this is: <span class="verse">"how the gold has become dim"</span> — the true <span class="heb-term">tzadik</span>, who is more precious than gold, has become dim, and his light has been darkened for us.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  And as our Sages, of blessed memory, said — that Yirmiyahu was lamenting <span class="verse">"how the gold has become dim"</span> over the passing of the <span class="heb-term">tzadik</span> Yoshiyahu. And so too, in every generation, it alludes to the passing and concealment of the light of the true <span class="heb-term">tzadik</span> of the generation. And this is: <span class="verse">"how the gold has become dim"</span> — that his light has been darkened for us, and we do not merit to benefit from his light.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  And it is not enough [that his light is hidden] — but our sorrow is compounded by more grief still. For <span class="verse">"the fine gold has changed"</span> <span class="source-ref">(Lamentations 4:1)</span> — the true <span class="heb-term">tzadik</span>, who is likened to fine gold, has had his light so thoroughly darkened from Israel that the truth itself has been completely changed. For <span class="verse">"they call evil good and good evil"</span> <span class="source-ref">(Isaiah 5:20)</span>. And this is <span class="verse">"the fine gold has changed"</span> — that the fine gold, which is the true <span class="heb-term">tzadik</span>, has been changed, for they speak all manner of evil about him and change and exchange the truth for falsehood.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  And through this: <span class="verse">"The holy stones are poured out at the head of every street"</span> <span class="source-ref">(Lamentations 4:1)</span>. This is said regarding the concealment of the <span class="heb-term">tzadik</span>, who is the aspect of the <span class="key-concept">head of the house</span> [<span class="heb-term">rosh bayis</span>]. And the <span class="heb-term">mefursamim shel sheker</span> [the falsely-famous ones] intensify — who are the aspect of <span class="verse">"head of every street"</span>, as is explained in the Torah teaching <span class="verse">"Beraishis–L'Einei"</span> etc. (see there, <span class="lm-ref">Likutay Moharan II, 67</span>).
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  And this is: <span class="verse">"The precious children of Zion"</span> <span class="source-ref">(Lamentations 4:2)</span> etc. — as is explained there in the eulogy on <span class="heb-term">Parashas Eileh Toldos Noach</span>, see there in the above-mentioned <span class="heb-term">siman</span>.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  And this is: <span class="verse">"Even jackals offer the breast"</span> <span class="source-ref">(Lamentations 4:3)</span> etc. — which is the aspect of the <span class="key-concept">compassion of the <span class="heb-term">sitra achra</span></span> [false compassion], as is explained in the Torah teaching <span class="verse">"Tik'u-Tochachah"</span> mentioned above (<span class="lm-ref">Likutay Moharan II, 8</span>). For through this, the aspect of <span class="verse">"and the serpent was cunning"</span> intensifies, G-d forbid — through which all the troubles mentioned above are drawn, until one does not know about the true <span class="heb-term">tzadik</span>. As is understood above: when one subdues the contamination of the serpent — which is the aspect of <span class="verse">"even jackals offer the breast"</span>, etc. — through the prayer of the <span class="heb-term">ba'al ko'ach</span>, then one merits all the levels mentioned above, until the <span class="heb-term">medameh</span> is refined through the true <span class="heb-term">tzadik</span>, as mentioned above. And the reverse, the reverse, G-d forbid [when the serpent intensifies]. And then one does not know: <span class="heb-term">Eichah</span>! Where is the light of the true <span class="heb-term">tzadik</span>? — which is drawn from the aspect of <span class="verse">"even jackals offer the breast"</span>, etc., as mentioned above.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  But through the lamentations and the crying "<span class="heb-term">Eichah</span>!" — we merit that his light should be revealed to us, and we merit complete <span class="heb-term">emunah</span>, until the song of the future is aroused — and then the joy will be very great. And as our Sages, of blessed memory, said: <span class="maxim">"Rejoice with her, rejoice — all who mourn over her"</span> <span class="source-ref">(Ta'anis 30b)</span>, etc.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  And this is the aspect of <span class="key-concept"><span class="heb-term">Shabbos Chazon</span></span>. <span class="heb-term">Chazon</span> [Vision] specifically — meaning, prophecy. For the primary rectification that we need now is to return and draw down the emanation of prophecy — through which the primary refinement of the <span class="heb-term">medameh</span> [is accomplished], through which the completeness of <span class="heb-term">emunah</span> [comes], as mentioned above. For on Shabbos is the primary rectification — for <span class="maxim">"Shabbos protected him"</span> — it protected Adam HaRishon, who blemished all the above. And <span class="maxim">"Shabbos protected him."</span> And therefore, this Shabbos before <span class="heb-term">Tisha B'Av</span> is called <span class="heb-term">Shabbos Chazon</span> — to indicate that we need now, on this Shabbos, to rectify the aspect of <span class="heb-term">emunah</span>, whose primary [source] depends on prophecy, as is explained in the Torah teaching mentioned above. And therefore it is called <span class="heb-term">Shabbos Chazon</span> — in the language of prophecy, as mentioned above.
</div>

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<!-- Section 6 (source: אות ו) — Names of Tzadikim  -->
<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<div class="section-number">§ 6 — The Names of the <i>Tzadikim</i></div>

<div class="paragraph">
  And this is the aspect of what <span class="heb-term">Rabbainu</span>, of blessed memory, wrote in <span class="heb-term">Sefer HaAlef-Bais HeChadash</span>, entry <span class="heb-term">Tzadik</span>, §20 — that through the <span class="key-concept">mentioning of the names of the <span class="heb-term">tzadikim</span></span>, one can bring about renewal in the work of Creation — that is, to change nature. For it is explained in the Torah teaching <span class="verse">"Tik'u-Tochachah"</span> mentioned above that every <span class="heb-term">tzadik</span> has the aspect of a spirit of prophecy, <span class="heb-term">ru'ach hakodesh</span> — through which the <span class="heb-term">medameh</span> of all those who draw close to him is refined. And through this, one merits the <span class="heb-term">emunah</span> of the renewal of the world. And through this <span class="heb-term">emunah</span>, there will be the renewal of the world in the future — when the world will be conducted in the aspect of <span class="heb-term">Eretz Yisrael</span>, meaning in the aspect of Providence and wonders, not in the way of nature — see there, all this is explained well.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  And therefore, through mentioning the names of the <span class="heb-term">tzadikim</span> — through this, the <span class="heb-term">reshimu</span> [residual imprint] of them is aroused, as <span class="heb-term">Rabbainu</span>, of blessed memory, wrote elsewhere (<span class="lm-ref">Likutay Moharan I, 248</span>) — that through telling stories of <span class="heb-term">tzadikim</span>, their <span class="heb-term">reshimu</span> is aroused. And therefore, through the mentioning of their names, the power of their <span class="heb-term">reshimu</span> and of their good deeds is aroused. And the primary power of the good deeds of the <span class="heb-term">tzadikim</span> is that through their good deeds, they merited the aspect of <span class="heb-term">ru'ach hakodesh</span>. And they drew down through this the <span class="heb-term">emunah</span> of the renewal of the world, as mentioned above.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  And therefore, through the mentioning of their names, one can certainly bring about change in the work of Creation — that is, to change nature. For through the mentioning of the names of the <span class="heb-term">tzadikim</span>, the power of their <span class="heb-term">ru'ach hakodesh</span> is aroused, and the <span class="heb-term">emunah</span> of the renewal of the world is drawn into the world. And through this, an illumination is drawn from the renewal of the world in the future — which will come about through this, as mentioned above. For then, the world will be conducted in the aspect of Providence and wonders, not in the way of nature. And therefore, one can certainly change nature through this.
</div>

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<!-- Section 7 (source: אות ז) — Pinchas             -->
<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<div class="section-number">§ 7 — Pinchas and the Names of the Families</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  And all of this is merited through the prayer in the aspect of the <span class="key-concept">judgment of the <span class="heb-term">ba'al ko'ach</span></span>, as is explained well in the Torah teaching mentioned above — that through the prayer of the <span class="heb-term">ba'al ko'ach</span>, one merits to make converts and to increase His glory, blessed be He, and to draw down prophecy — through which the <span class="heb-term">medameh</span> is refined. It emerges that the power of the <span class="heb-term">tzadikim</span> who refine the <span class="heb-term">medameh</span> is drawn from the prayer of the <span class="heb-term">ba'al ko'ach</span> mentioned above — through which one merits the spirit of prophecy — through which the <span class="heb-term">medameh</span> is refined, as mentioned above.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  And this is why <span class="key-concept"><span class="heb-term">Parashas</span> <span class="verse">"Se'u es rosh Bnei Yisrael"</span></span> <span class="source-ref">(Numbers 26:2)</span> is juxtaposed with <span class="heb-term">Parashas Pinchas ben Elazar</span>, etc. For Pinchas turned back the wrath of Hashem, blessed be He, and sweetened the judgment from Israel through prayer in the aspect of judgment, in the aspect of: <span class="verse">"And Pinchas stood and prayed, and the plague was stayed"</span> <span class="source-ref">(Psalms 106:30)</span>, as is explained well at the beginning of the Torah teaching mentioned above — see there.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  And therefore, immediately after this — after the verse mentions the great power of Pinchas, who turned back His wrath, etc. (all of which was through his prayer in the aspect of judgment, as mentioned above, through which all the levels mentioned above are accomplished — from which the <span class="heb-term">tzadikim</span> receive the spirit of prophecy, through which the <span class="heb-term">medameh</span> is refined, and one merits <span class="heb-term">emunah</span> and the renewal of the world of the future, which is the aspect of <span class="heb-term">Eretz Yisrael</span>; and for this reason, the mentioning of the names of the <span class="heb-term">tzadikim</span> is especially auspicious, as mentioned above) —
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  — and this is the aspect of <span class="heb-term">Parashas</span> <span class="verse">"Se'u es rosh Bnei Yisrael l'mishpechosam"</span> — where the <span class="key-concept">names of all the <span class="heb-term">tzadikim</span></span> are mentioned, who are the heads of the families of the children of Israel — in which Hashem, blessed be He, partnered His Name with their names. As it is written: <span class="verse">"HaChanochi, HaPalui"</span> — as Rashi explains: "My Name testifies upon them." It emerges that all the names of the families mentioned there in <span class="heb-term">Parashas Pinchas</span> are all the aspect of the names of the <span class="heb-term">tzadikim</span>, in which His Name, blessed be He, is partnered. And therefore, how good and beautiful is the juxtaposition of this <span class="heb-term">parsha</span> to the matter of Pinchas ben Elazar — who is the <span class="heb-term">ba'al ko'ach</span> who prayed the prayer in the aspect of judgment, from which the power of the <span class="heb-term">tzadikim</span> is drawn, etc. And for this reason, the mentioning of their names is especially auspicious, as mentioned above.
</div>

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<!-- Section 8 (source: אות ח) — Five Species         -->
<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<div class="section-number">§ 8 — Why <i>Netilas Yadayim</i> Only for the Five Species of Grain</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  And therefore, one is only obligated in <span class="heb-term">netilas yadayim</span> for bread over which one recites <span class="heb-term">HaMotzi</span> and <span class="heb-term">Birchas HaMazon</span>. And <span class="heb-term">HaMotzi</span> and <span class="heb-term">Birchas HaMazon</span> are only recited upon the <span class="key-concept">five species with which <span class="heb-term">Eretz Yisrael</span> was praised</span>. For the primary mitzvah of <span class="heb-term">Birchas HaMazon</span> is only to bless Him, blessed be He, for having given us <span class="heb-term">Eretz Yisrael</span> — as it is written: <span class="verse">"And you shall eat and be satisfied, and you shall bless Hashem your G-d for the good land"</span> <span class="source-ref">(Deuteronomy 8:10)</span>, etc.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  For the primary holiness of eating is through <span class="heb-term">Eretz Yisrael</span> — which is the aspect of the renewal of the world of the future, through which the <span class="key-concept">song of the future</span> is drawn — through which one merits that the eating should be in the aspect of <span class="heb-term">mezona d'nishmesa</span>, as mentioned above. And for this reason, the primary mitzvah of <span class="heb-term">netilas yadayim</span> is for this purpose, as mentioned above. And therefore, the primary <span class="heb-term">netilas yadayim</span> is for the five species specifically — which are obligated in <span class="heb-term">Birchas HaMazon</span>, which are the praise of <span class="heb-term">Eretz Yisrael</span>. For the primary [purpose of] <span class="heb-term">netilas yadayim</span> is to draw the aspect of <span class="heb-term">Eretz Yisrael</span> through the waters of <span class="heb-term">da'as</span> — in order to merit the song mentioned above, so that the eating should be in the aspect of <span class="heb-term">mezona d'nishmesa</span>, as mentioned above.
</div>

<div class="paragraph" style="text-align: center; font-style: italic; color: var(--accent-muted); margin-top: 1.5rem;">
  And there is still much more to say about this. Hashem, blessed be He, should grant us to draw complete <span class="heb-term">emunah</span> into the world, and may we return to <span class="heb-term">Eretz Yisrael</span> speedily in our days. And may there be fulfilled: <span class="verse">"You shall come, you shall gaze, from the peak of <span class="heb-term">Amanah</span>"</span> <span class="source-ref">(Song of Songs 4:8)</span> — speedily in our days, Amen.
</div>

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<!-- BETZI'AS HAPAS                                  -->
<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<div class="betzias-header">Betzi'as HaPas</div>
<div style="text-align: center; font-size: 0.95rem; color: var(--accent-muted); margin-bottom: 1.5rem; font-style: italic;">[Breaking the Bread]</div>

<!-- Section 9 (source: אות ט) — Five Species & Hei of HaShishi -->
<div class="section-number">§ 9 — The Five Species and the <i>Hei</i> of <i>HaShishi</i></div>

<div class="paragraph">
  And therefore they are the <span class="key-concept">five species</span> — corresponding to the <span class="heb-term">Hei</span> of <span class="verse">"<b>Ha</b>Shishi"</span> <span class="source-ref">(Genesis 1:31)</span>. For the entire world was in suspense until the sixth of Sivan, when Israel received the Torah — which is the aspect of prophecy, through which the renewal of the world was revealed, as is explained in the Torah teaching mentioned above. It emerges that the <span class="heb-term">Hei</span> of <span class="verse">"HaShishi"</span> indicates the renewal of the world. And from there is the primary holiness of <span class="heb-term">Eretz Yisrael</span>, which receives its holiness through <span class="verse">"the power of His deeds"</span> etc. — through knowing that Hashem, blessed be He, created the world, in the aspect of <span class="verse">"In the beginning, G-d created"</span> etc., as is explained there in the Torah teaching mentioned above.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  And from there — from the aspect of <span class="heb-term">Eretz Yisrael</span>, the aspect of the renewal of the world that was revealed through the <span class="heb-term">Hei</span> of <span class="verse">"HaShishi"</span> — from there, the five species that are the praise of <span class="heb-term">Eretz Yisrael</span> receive [their power]. For the five species correspond to the <span class="heb-term">Hei</span> of <span class="verse">"HaShishi"</span>, through which the primary holiness of <span class="heb-term">Eretz Yisrael</span> [comes]. From there the five species receive their power to nourish and satisfy a person in the aspect of <span class="heb-term">mezona d'nishmesa</span> — from which the primary true satiation [derives], in the aspect of: <span class="verse">"The righteous eats to satisfy his soul"</span> <span class="source-ref">(Proverbs 13:25)</span>.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  And therefore, the five species specifically have the power to satisfy a person. For they receive their power from <span class="heb-term">Eretz Yisrael</span>, from the aspect of the <span class="heb-term">Hei</span> of <span class="verse">"HaShishi"</span>, from the aspect of the <span class="heb-term">emunah</span> of the renewal of the world — from which <span class="heb-term">mezona d'nishmesa</span> is drawn, from which the primary satiation [derives]. For with <span class="heb-term">mezona d'gufa</span>, which is the aspect of the eating of Eisav, the eating of the <span class="heb-term">sitra achra</span> — it is said: <span class="verse">"And the belly of the wicked shall lack"</span> <span class="source-ref">(Proverbs 13:25)</span>. But <span class="heb-term">mezona d'nishmesa</span> — there is the primary satiation, in the aspect of <span class="verse">"the righteous eats to satisfy his soul"</span>. For <span class="heb-term">mezona d'nishmesa</span> is the aspect of <span class="verse">"Hashem is my shepherd, I shall not lack"</span> <span class="source-ref">(Psalms 23:1)</span>, the aspect of <span class="verse">"for there is no lack to those who fear Him"</span> <span class="source-ref">(Psalms 34:10)</span>, as is explained in the Torah teaching mentioned above — the opposite of <span class="heb-term">mezona d'gufa</span>, which is the aspect of the eating of the wicked, which is the aspect of <span class="verse">"the belly of the wicked shall lack"</span>, as mentioned above.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  And therefore, even in a physical sense, the primary satiation is through the five species — which are the primary bread that sustains the heart, upon which one is obligated in <span class="heb-term">HaMotzi</span> and <span class="heb-term">Birchas HaMazon</span>. For they are the five species that are the praise of <span class="heb-term">Eretz Yisrael</span>, in which the holiness of <span class="heb-term">Eretz Yisrael</span> is drawn — the aspect of the <span class="heb-term">emunah</span> of the renewal of the world, which was revealed through the <span class="heb-term">Hei</span> of <span class="verse">"HaShishi"</span> — and for this reason they are five species. And through the fact that they are in the aspect of <span class="heb-term">Eretz Yisrael</span>, etc. — through this, they are in the aspect of <span class="heb-term">mezona d'nishmesa</span> to a greater degree. And therefore, the primary satiation is through them, as mentioned above.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  And this is the aspect of the <span class="key-concept"><span class="heb-term">Hei</span> of <span class="heb-term">HaMotzi</span></span> — that one needs to articulate the <span class="heb-term">Hei</span> of <span class="verse">"<b>Ha</b>Motzi"</span>, as our Sages, of blessed memory, cautioned, and as the Holy Zohar greatly elaborates on the matter of the <span class="heb-term">Hei</span> of <span class="verse">"HaMotzi."</span> For the <span class="heb-term">Hei</span> of <span class="verse">"<b>Ha</b>Motzi"</span> is the aspect of the <span class="heb-term">Hei</span> of <span class="verse">"<b>Ha</b>Shishi"</span> — which indicates the renewal of the world, through which the primary rectification of eating in holiness is accomplished, in the aspect of <span class="heb-term">mezona d'nishmesa</span>, as mentioned above.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  And this is [the reason] that our Sages, of blessed memory, based the recitation of <span class="heb-term">HaMotzi</span> with a <span class="heb-term">Hei</span> upon the verse: <span class="verse">"<b>Ha</b>Motzi eschem mitachas sivlos Mitzrayim"</span> [<span class="verse">"Who brought you out from under the burdens of Egypt"</span>] <span class="source-ref">(Exodus 6:7)</span>. For in truth, it is all one. For the verse <span class="verse">"HaMotzi eschem"</span> etc. — meaning, the Exodus from Egypt — indicates the renewal of the world. For at the time of the Exodus from Egypt, the renewal of the world was revealed through the signs and wonders, as is brought in all the holy books. Also, the primary purpose of the Exodus from Egypt was for the receiving of the Torah, as it is written: <span class="verse">"When you bring the people out of Egypt, you shall serve"</span> etc. <span class="source-ref">(Exodus 3:12)</span>. And the primary revelation of the renewal of the world was through the receiving of the Torah, as mentioned above. It emerges that the verse <span class="verse">"HaMotzi eschem mitachas sivlos Mitzrayim"</span> indicates the renewal of the world. And therefore, from there our Sages, of blessed memory, derived the <span class="heb-term">Hei</span> of <span class="verse">"HaMotzi"</span> — which is the primary rectification — which indicates the renewal of the world, which is the primary rectification of eating in the aspect of <span class="heb-term">mezona d'nishmesa</span>, as mentioned above.
</div>

<!-- Section 10 (source: אות י) — Whole Bread -->
<div class="section-number">§ 10 — Reciting <i>HaMotzi</i> on Whole Bread</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  And this is why one needs to be precise about reciting <span class="heb-term">HaMotzi</span> upon <span class="key-concept">whole bread</span>. And the whole [loaf] has importance and takes precedence in law over the broken one. For the eating of Israel needs to be in the aspect of <span class="heb-term">mezona d'nishmesa</span>, which is the aspect of completeness without any lack, in the aspect of: <span class="verse">"Hashem is my shepherd, I shall not lack"</span> <span class="source-ref">(Psalms 23:1)</span> — which is said regarding <span class="heb-term">mezona d'nishmesa</span>, the aspect of <span class="verse">"for there is no lack to those who fear Him"</span> <span class="source-ref">(Psalms 34:10)</span>.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  And therefore, the whole bread has importance. For it is closer to the aspect of <span class="heb-term">mezona d'nishmesa</span>, which is complete without any lack, the aspect of <span class="verse">"for there is no lack to those who fear Him"</span>, as mentioned above.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  And therefore, in truth, the <span class="heb-term">pritzei amainu</span> <span class="heb-def">[the wayward among our people]</span> who go in the ways of the nations — they do not set out whole bread for their meal, but only slices, in the manner of the nations. For in all their gestures, they wish to show that they are uprooting themselves from the ways of Israel. For among us, there is importance to whole bread for <span class="heb-term">Birchas HaMotzi</span>, as it is written in the <span class="heb-term">Shulchan Aruch</span>. And these wicked ones reveal that all their sustenance is <span class="heb-term">mezona d'gufa</span>, the aspect of the eating of Eisav, the eating of the wicked — where there is no completeness. For their eating is in the aspect of <span class="verse">"the belly of the wicked shall lack"</span> <span class="source-ref">(Proverbs 13:25)</span>. For they have no <span class="heb-term">emunah</span>. And therefore they do not merit <span class="heb-term">mezona d'nishmesa</span>, which is drawn from <span class="heb-term">emunah</span>, as mentioned above.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  But the eating of Israel — the holy nation — is in the aspect of <span class="heb-term">mezona d'nishmesa</span>. For they are precise in their blessings, to bless Hashem, blessed be He, in their eating, with <span class="heb-term">Birchas HaMotzi</span> and <span class="heb-term">Birchas HaMazon</span> — all of which indicates the renewal of the world. And therefore, they are precise about reciting the blessing upon the whole [loaf] — which is the aspect of <span class="verse">"for there is no lack to those who fear Him"</span>, the aspect of <span class="heb-term">mezona d'nishmesa</span>, as mentioned above.
</div>

<div class="paragraph" style="text-align: center; font-weight: 600; color: var(--accent); margin-top: 2rem; padding: 0.5rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--border);">
  Blessed be Hashem forever, Amen and Amen.
</div>

<!-- Translator's Summary -->
<div class="translator-summary">
  <div class="summary-heading">✦ Translator's Summary — Part 2 ✦</div>

  <p style="margin-bottom:0.8rem;">
    This concluding portion of Halacha 4 mirrors the themes of Halacha 3 Part 2 but through the specific lens of <em>Tik'u Tochachah</em> (LM II:8), with its emphasis on the <em>ba'al ko'ach</em>'s prayer subduing the serpent's cunning, and the <em>mezona d'gufa</em>/<em>mezona d'nishmesa</em> duality.
  </p>

  <p style="margin-bottom:0.8rem;">
    <strong>Water and creation:</strong> Water preceded creation → contains the root of <em>da'as</em> of <em>chidush ha'olam</em> → hence all purification through water → hence all entry into holiness requires water.
  </p>

  <p style="margin-bottom:0.8rem;">
    <strong>Tisha B'Av:</strong> The same devastating reading of <em>Eichah</em> 4:1 — "the gold has become dim" = the <em>tzadik</em> is hidden; "the fine gold has <em>changed</em>" = truth inverted, good called evil and evil called good. The "holy stones poured out at the head of every street" = the <em>mefursamim shel sheker</em> (the falsely famous) occupy the public stage. "Even jackals offer the breast" = false compassion of the <em>sitra achra</em> (LM II:8).
  </p>

  <p style="margin-bottom:0.8rem;">
    <strong>Betzi'as HaPas — new material:</strong> The five species of grain correspond to the <em>Hei</em> of "<em>HaShishi</em>" (Genesis 1:31) — the world hung in suspense until the sixth of Sivan (Matan Torah), which revealed <em>chidush ha'olam</em>. From there → holiness of <em>Eretz Yisrael</em> → five species receive their nourishing power → <em>mezona d'nishmesa</em>. The <em>Hei</em> of <em>HaMotzi</em> = the <em>Hei</em> of <em>HaShishi</em> = indicates the renewal of the world. Derived from "<em>HaMotzi eschem mitachas sivlos Mitzrayim</em>" — for the Exodus (and the giving of the Torah that followed) revealed <em>chidush ha'olam</em>.
  </p>

  <p>
    <strong>Whole bread:</strong> <em>Mezona d'nishmesa</em> = completeness = "I shall not lack." Whole bread reflects this completeness. Those who abandon Jewish custom and serve only slices reveal their eating as <em>mezona d'gufa</em> — "the belly of the wicked shall lack."
  </p>
</div>


